  "typical_application": "RC relaxation oscillator: resistor from output to input, cap from input to ground, f ~ 1/(RC). Also squares slow/noisy signals and debounces switches. Tie all unused inputs to VSS or VDD.",
  "gotchas": [
    "CD40xx CMOS has weak output drive; do not drive LEDs or long lines directly, buffer first",
    "never leave CMOS inputs floating; tie unused gate inputs to a rail or they oscillate and draw current",
    "the 74HC14 is the faster, higher-drive 5V-centric equivalent but tops out at ~6V, while the 40106 runs to 18V",
    "oscillator frequency drifts with supply voltage because the thresholds scale with Vdd"
  ],
